From: thingino <thingino@opensensor>
Subject: [PATCH] mips/xburst/soc-t23/isvp/Pike: fix SOFT_I2C1_GPIO pin numbers

The stock Pike/board.h default for CONFIG_SOFT_I2C1_GPIO_V12_JZ
(GPIO_PB(25)/GPIO_PB(26)) is just a generic reference-SDK placeholder --
never actually exercised by any board in this tree until now, since no
board previously enabled CONFIG_SOFT_I2C1_GPIO_V12_JZ.

Reverse-engineered the real pin assignment for the Cinnado B6 T23ZN/TM18NA
LTE camera (cinnado_b6_t23zn_os02g10_tm18na) directly from the vendor's
shipped, boot-tested production kernel image ("Immortal" kernel from
firmware_T23ZN_20260803_2026.bin): the compiled-in `i2c1_gpio_data`
platform_data struct (the only actually-referenced/registered
CONFIG_I2C_GPIO platform_device in that image, confirmed via cross-
reference of the "i2c-gpio" name-string pointer) has sda_pin=53
(GPIO_PB(21)), scl_pin=52 (GPIO_PB(20)), udelay=5, timeout=1000 --
not the SDK default PB25/PB26. This is bus 1, matching how the vendor's
own `lp_mgr`/`mcu_test` binaries address the companion MCU as
`/dev/i2c-1`: on this board it's a GPIO-bitbanged bus, not the
I2C1_V12_JZ hardware controller (which uses fixed PB25/PB26 pins that
this board's MCU is not actually wired to).

Since GPIO_I2C1_SDA/SCK are compile-time-only under
CONFIG_SOFT_I2C1_GPIO_V12_JZ, and no other board in this tree enables
that symbol, this change is dead code everywhere else.

diff --git a/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t23/chip-t23/isvp/Pike/board.h b/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t23/chip-t23/isvp/Pike/board.h
--- a/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t23/chip-t23/isvp/Pike/board.h
+++ b/arch/mips/xburst/soc-t23/chip-t23/isvp/Pike/board.h
@@ -11,8 +11,8 @@
 #endif

 #ifdef CONFIG_SOFT_I2C1_GPIO_V12_JZ
-#define GPIO_I2C1_SDA GPIO_PB(25)
-#define GPIO_I2C1_SCK GPIO_PB(26)
+#define GPIO_I2C1_SDA GPIO_PB(21)
+#define GPIO_I2C1_SCK GPIO_PB(20)
 #endif

 #ifdef CONFIG_SOFT_I2C2_GPIO_V12_JZ
